It seems that we do not check if the dimension of data declared in the model is the same with that in the data passed in.  <div>In this example, essentially, the data declared in the model is [2, M],  but the real data have dimension [M, 2].</div>
<div><br></div><div>--</div><div>Jiqiang <br><br><br><div class="gmail_quote">---------- Forwarded message ----------<br>From: <b class="gmail_sendername">Rivka</b> <span dir="ltr">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel="nofollow">jvos...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span><br>
Date: Fri, Nov 9, 2012 at 2:50 PM<br>Subject: [stan-users] Estimating means of two multi variate normals<br>To: <a href data-email-masked rel="nofollow">stan-...@googlegroups.com</a><br><br><br><div style="font-size:medium;font-family:&#39;Times New Roman&#39;;min-height:1em">
<div style="min-height:1em"><div style="min-height:1em"><pre style="background-image:none;font-size:12.727272033691406px;line-height:2.8ex;white-space:pre-wrap;word-wrap:break-word">Hello,</pre><pre style="background-image:none;font-size:12.727272033691406px;line-height:2.8ex;white-space:pre-wrap;word-wrap:break-word">
<br></pre><pre style="background-image:none;font-size:12.727272033691406px;line-height:2.8ex;white-space:pre-wrap;word-wrap:break-word">Could anyone explain to me why the code below </pre><pre style="background-image:none;font-size:12.727272033691406px;line-height:2.8ex;white-space:pre-wrap;word-wrap:break-word">
<br></pre><pre style="background-image:none;font-size:12.727272033691406px;line-height:2.8ex;white-space:pre-wrap;word-wrap:break-word"><pre style="background-image:none;font-size:2.5ex;line-height:2.8ex;white-space:pre-wrap;word-wrap:break-word">
data {
  int&lt;lower=0&gt; M; // M=10
  vector[M] Y[2]; // first column contains values close to 0, second column contains values close to 20 	
  vector[M] ones; // generated in R as ones = rep(1,M)
  matrix[M,M] Sigma; // generated in R as Sigma = diag(M)
}
parameters{
real mu1;
real mu2;
}
model{
Y[1] ~ multi_normal(mu1*ones,Sigma);
Y[2] ~ multi_normal(mu2*ones,Sigma);
}</pre></pre><pre style="background-image:none;font-size:12.727272033691406px;line-height:2.8ex;white-space:pre-wrap;word-wrap:break-word"><br></pre><pre style="background-image:none;font-size:12.727272033691406px;line-height:2.8ex;white-space:pre-wrap;word-wrap:break-word">
gives me two chains, one for each mu, with a mean of about 10? I would expect a mean of 0 for the chain for mu1 and a mean of 20 for the chain for mu2. Indeed, when Y consists of only one column with values close to 20, I get a chain for mu with mean 20. Also, when I use </pre>
<pre style="background-image:none;font-size:12.727272033691406px;line-height:2.8ex;white-space:pre-wrap;word-wrap:break-word"><br></pre><pre style="background-image:none;font-size:12.727272033691406px;line-height:2.8ex;white-space:pre-wrap;word-wrap:break-word">
<pre style="background-image:none;font-size:2.5ex;line-height:2.8ex;white-space:pre-wrap;word-wrap:break-word">parameters{
vector[M] mu1;
vector[M] mu2;
}
model{
Y[1] ~ multi_normal(mu1,Sigma);
Y[2] ~ multi_normal(mu2,Sigma);
}</pre><pre style="background-image:none;font-size:2.5ex;line-height:2.8ex;white-space:pre-wrap;word-wrap:break-word"><br></pre><pre style="background-image:none;font-size:2.5ex;line-height:2.8ex;white-space:pre-wrap;word-wrap:break-word">
instead, I get M chains for mu1 with means close to 0 and M chains for mu2 with means close to 20, which makes sense. I have attached the R code (also including the session info) and the model text file, in case that might be helpful.</pre>
<pre style="background-image:none;font-size:2.5ex;line-height:2.8ex;white-space:pre-wrap;word-wrap:break-word"><br></pre><pre style="background-image:none;font-size:2.5ex;line-height:2.8ex;white-space:pre-wrap;word-wrap:break-word">
Any help would be very much appreciated!</pre><span><font color="#888888"><pre style="background-image:none;font-size:2.5ex;line-height:2.8ex;white-space:pre-wrap;word-wrap:break-word"><br></pre><pre style="background-image:none;font-size:2.5ex;line-height:2.8ex;white-space:pre-wrap;word-wrap:break-word">
Rivka</pre><div><br></div></font></span></pre></div></div></div><span><font color="#888888">

